// PARAM: --analysis interval
// No verdict annotations: a parse-rejection case. Every formal declares its
// kind. An unannotated parameter is not "untyped": it silently takes the
// compiler's default kind, so the actual bound to it converts to a width the
// source never names, and a caller reading the signature cannot tell which
// conversion happens.
int32 f(n) {
  return n
}
void main() {
  f(1)
}
